{{!
    @template tool_vae/structure_page

    The page "Archive de la structure", below its heading: a notification and the way back to the dossier; or the archive
    produced, with the link to download it; or, above the confirmation of the core that the page draws itself, what the
    archive is, who may read it and whether it replaces one in place.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\structure_page. The template holds no logic: the
    states exclude one another before. Every text and address is escaped (double braces), except three keys of HTML made by
    the core (triple braces): noticehtml and replaceshtml, notifications ($output->notification(); a refusal is escaped
    before); continuehtml, the button that goes back to the dossier ($output->continue_button()).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * intro - false, or a string: what the archive of the structure is
    * noticehtml - false, or HTML: the notification of the state (off, refused, produced, who may read the archive)
    * replaceshtml - false, or HTML: the notice that the archive replaces the one in place
    * download - false, or {url, label}: the link to download the archive produced
    * continuehtml - false, or HTML: the way back to the dossier

    Example context (json):
    {
        "intro": "The archive of the structure holds the positionings of the vaeiste, in a document of their own.",
        "noticehtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">Only the direction reads this archive.</div>",
        "replaceshtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-warning\">The new archive replaces the one in place.</div>",
        "download": {"url": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/5/tool_vae/structure/7/structure.zip", "label": "Download"},
        "continuehtml": "<div class=\"continuebutton\"><a href=\"https://example.com/dossier.php\">Continue</a></div>"
    }
}}
{{#intro}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{/intro}}
{{#noticehtml}}
{{{noticehtml}}}
{{/noticehtml}}
{{#replaceshtml}}
{{{replaceshtml}}}
{{/replaceshtml}}
{{#download}}
<a href="{{url}}" class="btn btn-primary">{{label}}</a>
{{/download}}
{{#continuehtml}}
{{{continuehtml}}}
{{/continuehtml}}
